URL: https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.56.0.tar.xz 596b02fea3d67e2ca45208aabebc92d2c14e7f2827f82cba59a630d55eea0854
URL: https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/git-2.56.0.tar.xz 596b02fea3d67e2ca45208aabebc92d2c14e7f2827f82cba59a630d55eea0854
Origname: git-2.56.0
Name: git

    git 2.56.0 with three Fil-C adaptations, carried over from the legacy
    projects/git-2.55.0 tree: (1) the parse-options defval fix: Fil-C
    pointers lose their capability when round-tripped through intptr_t, so
    storing string or pointer default values in 'intptr_t defval' compiles
    but crashes at runtime ("cannot read pointer with null object") as
    soon as the default is used (e.g. 'git status -u', 'git archive
    --add-file'); struct option's defval becomes void *, integer-valued
    option macros cast their defvals to (void *), string/pointer defvals
    are stored as real pointers, and integer use sites in parse-options.c,
    builtin/am.c and builtin/config.c cast back to intptr_t. (2) The
    compat/obstack fix: _obstack_begin/_obstack_begin_1 size every chunk
    at sizeof(struct _obstack_chunk) + alignment_mask (one object per
    chunk), _obstack_newchunk computes its size from the object being
    allocated, and obstack_blank always calls _obstack_newchunk instead of
    relying on chunk_limit - next_free pointer arithmetic. This disallows
    out-of-bounds writes between objects allocated via obstack; git always
    builds compat/obstack.o and uses it from kwset.c, which backs
    fixed-string 'git grep -F'. (3) config.mak sets NO_RUST = 1 to disable
    the Rust component (libgitcore), since there is no Fil-C Rust
    toolchain; the C fallback varint.o is compiled instead and the
    WITH_RUST code in help.c/repository.c compiles out. Upstream changed
    nothing relevant between 2.55.0 and 2.56.0 (compat/obstack is
    byte-identical, the Rust handling is the same, and only line-number
    drift in a few option tables needed fuzz), so the 2.55.0 patch applies
    in full and nothing had to be dropped. This used to be consumed as the
    legacy source tree projects/git-2.55.0; it is now a URL-based projeny
    project pointing at the official kernel.org release tarball, with the
    mirrors.edge.kernel.org copy as a fallback mirror.
